---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mural Prep on Textured Drywall in Florida | Surface Preparation"
  description="How to prep textured walls for murals in Central Florida. Orange peel, knockdown, and popcorn texture considerations."
  ogImage="/images/nemo-mural.jpg"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/mural-prep-textured-drywall-florida/#article",
        "headline": "Mural Prep on Textured Drywall in Florida",
        "description": "Surface prep for painting murals on textured walls common in Florida homes.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/mural-prep-textured-drywall-florida/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Mural Prep on Textured Drywall",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/mural-prep-textured-drywall-florida"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Mural Prep on Textured Drywall</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">Mural Prep on Textured Drywall in Florida</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        How to prep textured walls for murals. Orange peel, knockdown, and popcorn considerations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            Most <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, and Central Florida homes have textured drywall—orange peel, knockdown, or skip trowel. <a href="/services/murals" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Painting murals</a> on texture is possible, but prep work determines whether the mural looks crisp or rough. Here's how we handle it.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Types of Texture in Florida Homes</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Orange Peel (Light Texture)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Orange peel is the most common. It looks like fine bumps, similar to an orange rind. Light orange peel is mural-friendly—murals painted over light texture look fine with proper prep and primer.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Knockdown (Medium Texture)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Knockdown texture has flattened peaks and valleys. It shows through murals more than orange peel. Fine for hand-painted murals with bold designs, but detail work (faces, small characters) looks rough unless you skim coat smooth.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Skip Trowel or Heavy Texture</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Skip trowel, crow's foot, and other heavy textures create deep grooves. Murals painted over heavy texture look uneven and lose detail. These walls need skim coating to smooth before mural work.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Popcorn (Ceiling Texture)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Popcorn texture is rare on walls but common on ceilings. If you're painting a ceiling mural (stars, clouds), popcorn needs removal or skim coat. See our <a href="/guides/popcorn-ceiling-removal-kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">popcorn ceiling guide</a>.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Prep Options for Textured Walls</h2>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Option 1: Paint Over Texture (Light Texture Only)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            For light orange peel, we prep with primer and paint the mural directly over texture. The texture shows through slightly, which adds a hand-painted, artistic quality. This works well for:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Bold, graphic murals (jungle animals, space scenes, geometric designs)</li>
            <li>Kids room murals where slight texture adds charm</li>
            <li>Large character murals with simple shapes (Finding Nemo, Toy Story)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Pros:</strong> Faster, lower cost, texture adds character<br/>
            <strong>Cons:</strong> Fine details (faces, small text) look rough
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Option 2: Skim Coat Smooth</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Skim coating applies a thin layer of joint compound over the textured wall, then sands smooth. This creates a flat canvas for detailed mural work. Recommended for:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Detailed character murals with faces and fine lines</li>
            <li>Photo-realistic murals</li>
            <li>Medium to heavy texture (knockdown, skip trowel)</li>
            <li>Any mural where smooth finish matters</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Pros:</strong> Smooth finish, crisp details<br/>
            <strong>Cons:</strong> Adds 1-2 days and $2-$4/sq ft to project cost
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Option 3: Partial Skim Coat (Hybrid)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            For budget-conscious projects, we skim coat only the area where the mural will be painted, leaving surrounding walls textured. This keeps costs down while giving the mural a smooth base.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Texture adds character:</strong> Many Florida homeowners choose to paint murals over light texture. The slight roughness gives hand-painted murals a unique, artistic look that feels less "flat" than a smooth wall mural.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Step-by-Step Mural Prep on Textured Walls</h2>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Clean the Wall</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Wipe down the wall with a damp cloth to remove dust, cobwebs, and grease. Dirty walls prevent primer from adhering properly.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Repair Damage</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Fill any holes, cracks, or gouges with <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall compound</a>. Sand smooth and match surrounding texture if painting over texture. See our <a href="/guides/drywall-texture-matching-central-florida" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">texture matching guide</a>.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Prime the Surface</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Use a high-quality primer (we use Sherwin-Williams ProBlock or Benjamin Moore Fresh Start). Primer seals the texture, evens out absorption, and provides a uniform base for mural paint. Let dry 4-6 hours in Florida humidity.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Skim Coat (If Needed)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Apply thin layers of joint compound over texture using a 12" drywall knife. Let dry, sand smooth (220-grit), prime again. Skim coating adds 1-2 days to the timeline.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">5. Sketch the Mural</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Use pencil or chalk to sketch the mural design. On textured walls, use a softer pencil (2B or 4B) so lines show clearly over bumps.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">6. Paint the Mural</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Use quality interior <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">paint</a> (Benjamin Moore Regal Select or Sherwin-Williams Duration). Texture requires slightly more paint since it increases surface area. Budget 10-15% more paint for textured walls.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Cost Considerations</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Texture prep affects mural cost. Painting over light texture costs the same as smooth walls. Skim coating adds $2-$4 per square foot and 1-2 days to the project. See our <a href="/guides/kids-room-mural-ideas-kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">mural ideas guide</a> for full project costs.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">When to Leave Texture vs. Smooth</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Leave texture for:</strong> Bold graphic murals, jungle/space themes, large characters, kids rooms where texture adds charm.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Skim coat smooth for:</strong> Detailed portraits, photo-realistic murals, small intricate designs, nurseries with delicate themes, heavy knockdown or skip trowel texture.
          </p>

          <div class="text-center mt-12">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-6 font-sans">Ready to paint a mural on your textured walls?</p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Custom Murals on Textured Florida Walls"
    description="Proper prep for lasting murals. Serving Central Florida homeowners."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
